\begin_layout Plain Layout
Weight matrix
\end_layout

\end_inset


\begin_inset Separator latexpar
\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_deeper
\begin_layout Itemize
The weight matrix should capture the importance of all other regions for
 the i region (DI MAURO, PESARAN, 2013).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Determining the importance of one region to another is to determine the
 importance of one labor market to another labor market.
\end_layout

\begin_deeper
\begin_layout Itemize
Each region has its own labor market.
\end_layout

\begin_deeper
\begin_layout Itemize
Workers freely exchange markets.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
For a worker to move to another region, there must be a connection between
 those regions.
\end_layout

\end_deeper
\begin_layout Itemize
The importance of region j for region i will be a function of the connections
 between them.
\end_layout

\begin_deeper
\begin_layout Itemize
The connections are assumed to have an equal weight of importance.
\end_layout

\end_deeper
\end_deeper
\end_deeper
